{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-explainer-about-dragon-ball-including-dragon-ball-z-gt-and-super-explaining-what-the-st/audio/main-90d180c36afe.mp3","durationSec":185.472,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.74,"text":"Akira Toriyama was a Japanese manga artist."},{"start":3.22,"end":6.84,"text":"He wrote and drew the Dragon Ball manga from 1984 to 1995."},{"start":6.84,"end":10.76,"text":"Manga means a Japanese comic, and it came before the anime."},{"start":11.54,"end":13.64,"text":"The early story follows Goku as a boy."},{"start":14.18,"end":16.8,"text":"He lives far from towns until he meets Bulma."},{"start":17.32,"end":19.14,"text":"They look for seven magical Dragon Balls."},{"start":19.84,"end":22.54,"text":"Together, the balls can call a dragon that gives one wish."},{"start":23.2,"end":28.26,"text":"Goku also trains in martial arts with Master Roshi, makes friends, and enters fighting tournaments."},{"start":28.72,"end":34.54,"text":"The first Dragon Ball anime ran from 1986 to 1989 and showed this early story."},{"start":34.54,"end":37.88,"text":"Dragon Ball Z continued the later part of the manga."},{"start":38.6,"end":41.32,"text":"The anime ran from 1989 to 1996."},{"start":41.96,"end":47.5,"text":"It began about five years after the first anime, so Goku was now a young adult and a father."},{"start":48.22,"end":49.54,"text":"His son was named Gohan."},{"start":50.08,"end":55.34,"text":"An alien called Raditz told Goku that he was a Saiyan, a warrior from another planet."},{"start":56.32,"end":63.24,"text":"Goku then faced much stronger enemies, including the space tyrant Frieza and the magical being Majin Buu."},{"start":63.58,"end":68.54,"text":"The story became larger: Goku and his friends often fought to defend Earth."},{"start":68.54,"end":71.44,"text":"Gohan also trained and became stronger."},{"start":72.46,"end":76.04,"text":"Dragon Ball GT was a Toei anime with 64 episodes."},{"start":76.72,"end":82.36,"text":"It ran from 1996 to 1997, after Z, but it was not based on Toriyama’s manga."},{"start":83.06,"end":85.64,"text":"Toriyama described it as a grand side story."},{"start":86.8,"end":90.46,"text":"At the beginning, a wish changed adult Goku back into a child."},{"start":91.16,"end":93.9,"text":"He travelled through space with his granddaughter Pan and Trunks."},{"start":94.5,"end":99.56,"text":"They searched for the Black Star Dragon Balls because Earth would explode in one year if they failed."},{"start":100.38,"end":103.68,"text":"Later, Goku fought enemies such as Baby and the Shadow Dragons."},{"start":104.42,"end":108.74,"text":"GT was one possible continuation after Z, but it was separate from Super."},{"start":109.74,"end":112.48,"text":"Dragon Ball Super was another continuation after Z."},{"start":113.26,"end":121.2,"text":"Its anime ran from 2015 to 2018, and its story began after Majin Buu’s defeat, during the ten-year gap at the end of Z."},{"start":122.32,"end":127.02,"text":"Super is part of the main line, meaning it is treated as the main continuation of the story."},{"start":128.5,"end":130.7,"text":"Goku met Beerus, a God of Destruction."},{"start":131.56,"end":133.7,"text":"He also learned that other universes existed."},{"start":134.44,"end":138.8,"text":"In the Tournament of Power, fighters from different universes competed against one another."},{"start":139.44,"end":145.96,"text":"Z often focused on protecting Earth, but Super made the setting much bigger by adding gods and many universes."},{"start":147.02,"end":152.06,"text":"A simple comparison uses three ideas: starting point, big change, and result."},{"start":153.08,"end":157.38,"text":"Dragon Ball starts with Goku as a child, and his search for the seven balls begins his adventure."},{"start":157.94,"end":161.98,"text":"Z shows him as an adult and father, while battles for Earth become central."},{"start":162.84,"end":166.24,"text":"GT changes Goku into a child again and sends him into space."},{"start":166.92,"end":168.72,"text":"It is a separate side continuation."},{"start":169.8,"end":174.38,"text":"Super continues the main line after Buu and introduces gods and other universes."},{"start":175.5,"end":179.54,"text":"Therefore, the order is not simply Dragon Ball, Z, GT, and then Super."},{"start":180.44,"end":184.86,"text":"Both GT and Super follow Z, but they take different story roads."}],"words":[{"text":"Akira","start":0,"end":0.46},{"text":"Toriyama","start":0.46,"end":1.12},{"text":"was","start":1.12,"end":1.36},{"text":"a","start":1.36,"end":1.54},{"text":"Japanese","start":1.54,"end":1.92},{"text":"manga","start":1.92,"end":2.28},{"text":"artist","start":2.28,"end":2.74},{"text":"He","start":3.22,"end":3.28},{"text":"wrote","start":3.28,"end":3.48},{"text":"and","start":3.48,"end":3.64},{"text":"drew","start":3.64,"end":3.86},{"text":"the","start":3.86,"end":4.02},{"text":"Dragon","start":4.02,"end":4.34},{"text":"Ball","start":4.34,"end":4.52},{"text":"manga","start":4.52,"end":4.8},{"text":"from","start":4.8,"end":5.04},{"text":"1984","start":5.04,"end":5.66},{"text":"to","start":5.66,"end":6.02},{"text":"1995","start":6.02,"end":6.84},{"text":"Manga","start":6.84,"end":7.92},{"text":"means","start":7.92,"end":8.24},{"text":"a","start":8.24,"end":8.42},{"text":"Japanese","start":8.42,"end":8.8},{"text":"comic","start":8.8,"end":9.22},{"text":"and","start":9.66,"end":9.74},{"text":"it","start":9.74,"end":9.86},{"text":"came","start":9.86,"end":10.02},{"text":"before","start":10.02,"end":10.32},{"text":"the","start":10.32,"end":10.48},{"text":"anime","start":10.48,"end":10.76},{"text":"The","start":11.54,"end":11.68},{"text":"early","start":11.68,"end":11.92},{"text":"story","start":11.92,"end":12.24},{"text":"follows","start":12.24,"end":12.7},{"text":"Goku","start":12.7,"end":12.96},{"text":"as","start":12.96,"end":13.3},{"text":"a","start":13.3,"end":13.44},{"text":"boy","start":13.44,"end":13.64},{"text":"He","start":14.18,"en